requires-expression with a type requirement constraining a partial
specialization ([expr.prim.req.type]/1, [temp.constr]).

Was KNOWNBUG since round 152 (no diagnostic before the drop): the type
requirement `typename T::value_type` THREW for T = int, the constraint
evaluation caught the exception and took the constraint as satisfied, so the
specialization was selected for int and its member typedef failed.  Fixed
2026-09-23: an invalid type makes the requirement false.
